  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sanjay Singh vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. ... on 22 May, 2024 Author: Abdul Moin Bench: Abdul Moin High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:38739 Court No. - 6 Case :- Writ - A No. - 3950 of 2024 Petitioner :- Sanjay Singh Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Food Safety Drug Administration, Lk Counsel for Petitioner :- Mahendra Pratap Singh,Ranjit Singh Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Abdul Moin,J. 1. Heard. 2. Admittedly, against the order of punishment dated 09.04.2023, the petitioner has a statutory remedy of filing of an appeal before the appellate authority. Sanjay Singh vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. ... on 22 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/11915094/ 1 4. The aforesaid argument is patently fallacious inasmuch as it is settled provision of law that an appeal would lie to a still higher authority than the authority who has passed the order impugned.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for the petitioner contends that as it is the Head of Department i.e. the Commissioner, who has passed the order impugned consequently no appeal would lie as the order itself has been passed by the appellate authority."
  },
